# opm — package manager
File: website/pulled/opm.oot

Source: openOODA/opm/docs/

## What it is

The openOODA package manager. Tag v0.8.8. Packages are
content-addressed. Each package declares the caps it needs.
`add` refuses extra caps. That is the unique move.

Entry is `opm <subcommand>`. `ooda opm` spawns this binary.

## Install

```
curl -fsSL https://openooda.org/install.sh | bash
```

## Surface

Live commands from `opm/docs/cli.oot`:

| Command | Purpose |
|---------|---------|
| `add` | Resolve and install |
| `audit` | Walk the lock |
| `sbom` | CycloneDX-lite from the lock |
| `bot` | Verify a registry folder |
| `ingest` | Lock a file-backed recipe |
| `init` | Write starter `ooda.pkg` |
| `launch` | Re-verify a pinned payload |
| `remove` | Drop a package from the lock |
| `update` | Re-resolve the lock |
| `outdated` | List newer compatible versions |
| `why` | Why a package is in the lock |
| `pack` | Offline pack from the lock |
| `pkg` | Print the current lock |
| `publish` | Write to a local registry tree |
| `reg` | List or edit HTTPS stores |
| `search` | Search added stores |
| `tree` | Print a dep tree |
| `vendor` | List the file vendor |
| `clean` | Drop CAS dirs not in the lock |

HTTPS fetch needs `OODA_CURL`. Git clone needs `OODA_GIT`.
Compiler spawn needs `OODA_COMPILER`. Missing token is Err.
